ttext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Note then }{\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 WCF}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  summary in 7.4-6) \par }\pard \ql \li2160\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 fewer}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  in number, and administered with }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 more}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  simplicity, and }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 less}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  outward glory, \par yet, in them, it is held forth in }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 more}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 fullness}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 , }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 evidence}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  and }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 spiritual}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  efficacy, to }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 all}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  nations.\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Discontinuity: \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gal. 3:15-17}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Brothers and sisters, I give an example from daily life: once a person's will has been ratified, no one adds to it or annuls it.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 16}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Now the promises were made to Abraham and to his offspring; it does not say, \ldblquote And to offsprings,\rdblquote  as of many; but it says, \ldblquote And to your offspring,\rdblquote  that is, to one person, who is Christ.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 17}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  My point is this: the law, which came four hundred thirty years later, does not annul a covenant previously ratified by God, so as to nullify the promise.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 18}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  For if the inheritance comes from the law, it no longer comes from the promise; but God granted it to Abraham through the promise.}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li990\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin990\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 Principle of Discontinuity in WCF: \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1440\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls40\ilvl1\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 No longer under the law (works righteousness principle)  as temporal \ldblquote covenant\rdblquote  (Mosaic) or even as a eternal covenant (Creation) \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \u-3929\'a7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx2160\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls40\ilvl2\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 E.g. Temporal (Geo.Political works-righteousness conditioned)  vs. Eternal (Heavenly faith-righteousness conditioned) (}{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 Gal 3:19-29}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346  \ldblquote no longer Nation \ldblquote Jew\rdblquote  vs. \ldblquote Greek\rdblquote , }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 Gal 4:1ff}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 \emdash not according to \ldblquote elemental spirits\rdblquote  (seasons, etc), \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \u-3929\'a7\tab}E.g. Fulfillment Motif:  Shadows/Types vs. Real/Antitype (}{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346 Mt. 5:17, Heb. 10:1ff}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid11369346  \ldblquote only a shadow\rdblquote ...) WCF \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Explanation: Now what is very clear by the above two passages by way of comparison is this.  \par }{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par 1. Whatever the "law" is for Paul, it was that which came after the covenant made with Abraham and }{\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 not such as to annul}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  that previous covenant.  I.e. For Paul, the "law" (nomos) was exclusively used in reference to the covenant transacted through Moses whereby "old" covenant references "previous to present/new covenant."  As we shall see, it will be a great mistake then to equate "law" as Paul uses it with merely "works," although there was most certainly a "works" aspect to the "law" which related to the benefits and curses of the old covenant, especially in a typolical application with respect to the benefits of land, etc.   I.e. Paul's "law" is a covenantal term, less a term that describes "works" vs. "grace."  For Paul, "law" is synonymous with "Sinai Covenant." \par \par 2. There is something relative to the Mosaic covenant that has ceased, but not so as to annul the Abrahamic covenant that was according to Paul kept in tact in the Mosaic covenant.     This is also illustrated by the author of Hebrews: \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Heb. 10:1}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Since the law has only a shadow of the good things to come and not the true form of these realities, it can never, by the same sacrifices that are continually offered year after year, make perfect those who approach.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 2}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Otherwise, would they not have ceased being offered, since the worshipers, cleansed once for all, would no longer have any consciousness of sin?  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 3}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  But in these sacrifices there is a reminder of sin year after year.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 4}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  For it is impossible for the blood of bulls and goats to take away sins.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 5}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Consequently, when Christ came into the world, he said, \ldblquote Sacrifices and offerings you have not desired, but a body you have prepared for me;  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 6}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  in burnt offerings and sin offerings you have taken no pleasure.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 7}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Then I said, \lquote See, God, I have come to do your will, O God\rquote   (in the scroll of the book it is written of me).\rdblquote   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 8}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  When he said above, \ldblquote You have neither desired nor taken pleasure in sacrifices and offerings and burnt offerings and sin offerings\rdblquote   (these are offered according to the law),  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 9}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  then he added, \ldblquote See, I have come to do your will.\rdblquote  He abolishes the first in order to establish the second.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 10}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  And it is by God's will that we have been sanctified through the offering of the body of Jesus Christ once for all.\par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par See also Romans 7:1-6\par }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Note:  Other  Biblical Support For Understanding the Sinai Covenant In A Typological Way\par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1. The nation, land and people as numerous as sand are }{\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 typologically}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  fulfilled under the covenant of Moses\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1 Kings 4:20-21-- note that Abraham is the Father of Israel, Abraham's blessing is typified in Israel's favored status as sovereignly chosen out from other nations as a "holy nation."  \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 2. Mosaic covenant "typifies" the "covenant of creation based upon the meritorious actions of representative Adam in that all the temporal blessings of land, national status and covenant membership is based upon the principle of works. (See also Galatians  \par 3. Mosaic covenant "typifies" the covenant with Abraham in that a sacrificial substitute is being offered. (Lev.16:13-15)\par 4. Mosaic covenant retains the "sign" of circumcision\par 5. Mosaic covenant was self-consciously "temporal" as in Dt.4:1, Dt. 18:15-16.   \par 6. Mosaic covenant "typified" the New Covenant in continuity with Abrahamic... \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Acts 3:22 (Dt.18:15-16)-- Moses declared the coming of another lawgiver like unto himself  (See then Rom.10:5-8) \par a. The Nation of Israel is the church in NT(Rom.9:6-8)\par b. The Land of Israel is Heaven in the NT (Heb12:22-24)\par c. People of nations is the 'assembly of the first born" (Heb.12:23) the "remnant and the sands of the sea" (Rom.9:27) \par d. The veil guarding entrance into the "holy of holies" and the sympolic presence of god-- which contained an embroidered picture of the cherephim with swords) is torn upon in NC (Heb.10:19-20)\par e. Christ become the once and for all substitute for the propitiation of God's wrath against sin(Heb.9:23ff) \par f. Christ become the one typofied by one like Moses (Rom.10:5-8) so as to circumcise the heart. (Dt.9:4, 30:11-14)\par g. Baptism, as a sign of judgment  replaces circumcision (Col.2:11ff)\par h. The Lord's Day, as the day of New creation, replaces the "sabbath" as instituted in Creation... I.e. a return to the presence of God as through the sword of God's judgment... \par i. The Old Covenant (typological/temporal under Moses) is no longer operative.}{\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  \par \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0 {\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Therefore, the Mosaic covenant (old in relation to the new) is in discontinuity with new covenant along geo-political lines but in continuity with respect to the shared Abrahamic line. (See chart)\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1. Discontinuity with temporal aspects of the Mosaic law-- Gal.2:19, 3:24, 4:21ff\par 2. Continuity with the promisory aspects from the line of Seth through Abrahamic through Mosaic to Christ (Gal.3:14-18) \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 So here is the principle that will unlock the mystery of continuity and discontinuity.  There is in short a temporal aspect to the Mosaic covenant that has ceased, even as there is an eternal aspect of the Mosaic covenant in continuity with the promise made to Abraham and even Adam before him that remains as fulfilled by Christ.  For when God promised a "seed" who would guarantee the creation covenant stipulation on behalf of the elect, this was again ratified to Abraham in the covenant rite of the slain animals.  This promise did not annul the creation covenant based upon works, it merely added to this creation covenant the promise of substitution whereby God's grace would be revealed so as to be in harmony with his justice.  We should not then think in terms of "covenant of grace" vs. "covenant of works"-- rather we should think in terms of a COVENANT between God and humanity, a covenant that we have broken by our willful disobedience such as to deserve the curse of the covenant.  This covenant was never annuled.  Rather God added to the covenant a promise to meet its demands on behalf of those chose by his sovereign grace.   \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par III. Covenant in Redemptive History APPLIED! (The Principle of Continuity/Discontinuity Applied) \par \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Aspects of Continuity: \par }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080\faauto\ls37\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Salvation by Grace through Faith Alone\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 WCF 7.4:}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  This covenant of grace is frequently set forth in Scripture by the name of a testament, in reference to the death of Jesus Christ the Testator, and to the everlasting inheritance, with all things belonging to it, therein bequeathed.\par \par }{\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 WCF 7.6}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  ... There are not therefore two covenants of grace, differing in substance, but one and the same, under various dispensations.\par \par }{\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 WCF 11.6}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  The justification of believers under the old testament was, in all these respects, one and the same with the justification of believers under the new testament.\par }{\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par c.f. Above Illus. in Galatians, also Romans 4\par \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080\faauto\ls37\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 A Salvation of Mediated \ldblquote Presence\rdblquote  (Temple Theology) (C.F. Preston Graham Jr, A Sacramental Theology of the Gospel, in }{\b\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The Assembling of Ourselves Together, ed. John Vance (2005) }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 WCF 7.5}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  This covenant was differently administered in the time of the law, and in the time of the gospel: under the law it was administered by promises, prophecies, sacrifices, circumcision, the paschal lamb, and other types and ordinances delivered to the people of the Jews, all foresignifying Christ to come; which were, for that time, sufficient and efficacious, through the operation of the Spirit, to instruct and build up the elect in faith in the promised Messiah, by whom they had full remission of sins, and eternal salvation; and is called the old Testament.}{\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par \par }\pard\plain \s23\ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 \b\f27\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b0\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 In the language of Thomas Torrance, the church is nothing less than \ldblquote Christ\rquote s \ldblquote vis-\u224\'88-vis in history!\rdblquote   In the Old Testament, it is the church of God\rquote s presence in the temple of Creation, Bethel and Jerusalem.  In the New Testament, it is the church of God\rquote s presence linked to the ascended ministry of Christ acting through the Holy Spirit given at Pentecost and the formation of the New Covenant temple, even the church of a living God.  So then, for instance, Thomas Torrance has remarked how \ldblquote we cannot pay too much attention to the fact that the Holy Spirit was sent upon the church after the crucifixion, resurrection and the ascension of Christ.  In that series Pentecost belongs as one of the mighty salvation events, and to that series the parousia will belong as the last.\rdblquote }{\cs17\b0\f26\fs22\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f5\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs17\fs18\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  T. F. Torrance, }{\i\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Royal Priesthood, }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 (Edinburgh: Oliver and Boyd LTD, 1955), p. 23. }}}{\b0\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525    Applied then to the ministry of the church, Torrance continues:\par \par }\pard \s23\ql \li2160\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b0\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The spirit operates by creating out of the word a body that St. Paul calls the Body of Christ\u8230\'c9. It is the sphere where through the presence of the Spirit the salvation-events of the birth, life, death, resurrection and ascension are operative here and now in history, the sphere wherever within the old creation the new creation has broken in with power.\rdblquote }{\cs17\b0\f26\fs22\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f5\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs17\fs18\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Ibid, p.23. }}}{\b0\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard\plain \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 \f5\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 God\rquote s salvation of a people is first and foremost}{\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  not}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  presented as a logically ordered series of propositions, or merely as stories about the existential and personal quests for meaning on the part of individuals.   God\rquote s salvation of a people is revealed by a unified corporate history, one that is most essentially about God in the midst of His people-- a corporate fellowship with God!  As such Leslie Newbigin remarks how\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1980\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1980\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The Bible is not the story of ideas about God, but the story of the people of God\u8230\'c9the gospel does not come to each of us in isolation.  It comes to us through a particular book and through a particular fellowship\u8230\'c9 it is a false spirituality, divorced from the whole teaching of the Bible which regards this visible and continuing church as of subordinate importance for the life of Christ\u8230\'c9 God meets us through his people here and now in the form of an actual invitation into the fellowship of a body of people calling themselves one Church?}{\cs17\fs22\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f5\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs17\fs18\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Leslie Newbigin, }{\i\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The Reunion of the Church}{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 , (NY, NY: Harper & Row, 1948)p. 27, 29}}}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The gospel according to Paul is not a transition from temple to \ldblquote no temple\rdblquote  as some would have it.  In this regard, Paul's teaching for us under the New Covenant is no different than the prophetic teaching under the Old Covenant, that salvation is described with the promise " I will dwell with them" (2 Cor. 6:16). This is also Paul\rquote s point in 1 Corinthians 3, even as }{\f25\fs22\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Richard Hayes has observed, \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Paul dares to assert [that] the community is the place where God dwells. "Do you not know," he asks, "that you [plural] are God's temple and that God's Spirit dwells in you [plural]?"(3:16). To read this last sentence as though it spoke of the Spirit dwelling in the body of the individual Christian would be to miss the force of Paul's audacious metaphor: the apostolically founded community takes the place of the Jerusalem temple as the place where the glory of God resides.}{\cs17\fs22\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f5\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs17\fs18\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Richard B. Hayes, }{\i\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Eccesiology and Ethics in 1Corinthians}{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 , (located on the web. )N.p. }}}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 NT, see below temple\rdblquote  \par \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080\faauto\ls37\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 A Salvation Mediated in Prophetic, Priestly and Kingly Aspects corresponding to \ldblquote Word (}{\b\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Confessionalism}{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ), Ritual Worship (}{\b\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Sacramentalism}{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ), Governed Covenant Community (}{\b\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Communalism}{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 )  \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 WCF 7.6}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Under the gospel, when Christ, the substance, was exhibited, the ordinances in which this covenant is dispensed are the preaching of the Word, and the administration of the sacraments of Baptism and the Lord's Supper: which, though fewer in number, and administered with more simplicity, and less outward glory, yet, in them, it is held forth in more fullness, evidence, and spiritual efficacy, to all nations, both Jews and Gentiles; and is called the new Testament. There are not therefore two covenants of grace, differing in substance, but one and the same, under various dispensations.}{\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Aspects of Discontinuity: Related to Nation/Temporal (Geo/Political) vs. Spiritual (not to be confused with non-visual, but \ldblquote kingdom not of this world) (Heaven/Ecclesial) \par }{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Illustrated in Galatians:}{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  What remains and what does not?  The principle seems to be Paul's point later in Galations. (See also Rom.7:7ff)\par }{\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gal. 3:19ff }{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Why then the law? It was added because of transgressions, until the offspring would come to whom the promise had been made\u8230\'c9}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 21}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Is the law then opposed to the promises of God? Certainly not! For if a law had been given that could make alive, then righteousness would indeed come through the law\u8230\'c9}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 23}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Now before faith came, we were imprisoned and guarded under the law until faith would be revealed.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 24}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Therefore the law was our disciplinarian until Christ came, so that we might be justified by faith.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 25}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  But now that faith has come, we are no longer subject to a disciplinarian,  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 26}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  for in Christ Jesus you are all children of God through faith.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 27}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  As many of you as were baptized into Christ have clothed yourselves with Christ.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 28}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\i\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 There is no longer Jew or Greek, there is no longer slave or free, there is no longer male and female; for all of you are one in Christ Jesus.}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 29}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  And if you belong to Christ, then you are Abraham's offspring, heirs according to the promise. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Gal. 4:1}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   My point is this: heirs, as long as they are minors, are no better than slaves, though they are the owners of all the property;  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 2}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  but they remain under guardians and trustees until the date set by the father.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 3}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\i\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 So with us; while we were minors, we were enslaved to the elemental spirits of the world.}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 4}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  But when the fullness of time had come, God sent his Son, born of a woman, born under the law,  Formerly, when you did not know God, you were enslaved to beings that by nature are not gods.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 9}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Now, however, that you have come to know God, or rather to be known by God, how can you turn back again to the weak and beggarly }{\i\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 elemental spirits}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ? How can you want to be enslaved to them again?  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 10}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  You are }{\i\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 observing special days, and months, and seasons, and years.}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 11}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  I am afraid that my work for you may have been wasted.}{\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 If one follows the above argument of Paul, with special note of the italics-- it seems clear that Paul's principle in determining continuity from discontinuity is that of temporal vs. spiritual.  E.g. the "elemental spirits of the world."  This is related then to Paul's assertion that we are no longer "Jew or Greek" which is to say a geo-political identity, but rather our identity is in Christ who is the succession to the promise as revealed through Abraham. \par }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par ( c.f. Addendum: \ldblquote Temporal/Spiritual Illustrated in Genesis 15 and 17\rdblquote ) \par \par Applied: \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls38\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Covenant Community:  (note Hans LaRondelle, }{\b\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The Israel of God in Prophecy) }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1440\faauto\ls38\ilvl1\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 OT: Nation of Israel (Civil, Geographical) \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}NT: Church \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls3\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls3\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rom. 9... }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \ldblquote not all Israel is Israel...}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 That when Paul applies this passage, he applies it to the church\emdash that institution that is neither political or geographcial, but rather follows after Abraham by faith.  \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs18\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gal. 3:7}{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  so, you see, those who believe are the descendants of Abraham. \par }{\f25\fs18\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gal. 3:8}{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  And the scripture, foreseeing that God would justify the Gentiles by faith, declared the gospel beforehand to Abraham, saying, \ldblquote All the Gentiles shall be blessed in you.\rdblquote  \par }{\f25\fs18\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gal. 3:9}{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  For this reason, those who believe are blessed with Abraham who believed. \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls15\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls15\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Peter also applies this passage so as to apply to those of all nations who put their trust in Christ as being the descendents of Abraham\u8230\'c9 \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs18\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Acts 3:25 }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\b\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 You}{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  are the descendants of the prophets and of the covenant that God gave to your ancestors, saying to Abraham, \lquote }{\i\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 And in your descendants all the families of the earth shall be blessed.\rquote  \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\tx90\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\tx90{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls2\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Moreover, Peter specially refers to the church as the fulfillment of the \ldblquote nation\rdblquote  established by God through Abraham using language that was used to describe Israel under the Sinai period. \par }\pard\plain \s20\ql \li1890\ri0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1890\itap0\pararsid742525 \f2\fs20\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\f25\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1Pet. 2:9}{\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  But you are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, a holy }{\b\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 nation}{\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 , His own special people, that you may proclaim the praises of Him who called you out of darkness into His marvelous light;\par }{\b\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 nation,people\u8230\'c9}{\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ;\par }\pard\plain \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\tx90{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 \f5\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls2\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Paul then in Rom. 9 specifically states that there are two kinds of Israel\rquote s\emdash one of the political/geographical type, the other of a more spiritual type, whose politic is spiritual and whose land is heavenly\u8230\'c9 \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rom. 9:6- They are not all Israel who are of Israel. Nor are they all children because they are the seed of Abraham\u8230\'c9 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 He goes on to say that God never forsook true, spiritual Israel, but only that Israel that was political/geographical only.   God will restore Israel, but again an Israel that will be conveened in heaven as it where.\par }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls38\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Entrance Rite: (note: Meredith Kline, }{\b\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 By Oath Consigned)}{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1440\faauto\ls38\ilvl1\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 OT: Circumcision\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}NT: Baptism\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}\par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The trajectory of a entrance rite in a system of passing through judgment into salvation. \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 As a "sign," there is no doubt as from the teachings of the apostles that baptism today means precisely what circumcision meant in it's day, albeit signified by different elements (as is also the case with the Lord's supper in relation to Passover)  So we see Peter relating "baptism" to the waters of both the Red sea and Noah's flood as signs of passing through a great judgment ordeal.  Apart from God's saving covenant, this would be to pass through judgement into punishment.  Yet within God's saving covenant, this meant passing through the judgment waters into salvation even as God protected them from the covenant enemies.  And of course, the sign of "water" was then exactly that of the sign of a "knife" in the cutting ceremony of circumcision.  Even the waters of Noah's flood are described as a "berith" which is the word for covenant making as derived from the verb "to cut."   See for yourself as you reflect upon the following passages of scripture.\par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  \par }\pard \qj \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Genesis 3:24\par }\pard \qj \li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The sword imagery is first depicted in Genesis 3:24 where the judgment sword was given to the cherubim after Adam and Eve's expulsion from the sanctuary of the garden.  Meredith Kline states, "In the hour that God drove man into exile it was indicated that any future return to God's dwelling place and the tree of life must involve a passage through the flaming sword of God's judgment." (Meridith Kline, Kingdom Prologue, p.85) This image is later placed upon the great curtains which guarded the Holy of Holies from intrusion.  However, on the day of Atonement the blood from a sacrificial substitute  was sprinkled upon the cover of the ark as representing the passing through God's judgment into his Holy presence by means of a representative substitute.  Therefore, participation in the rite of circumcision as depicted in Genesis 15, 17, and 22   represented a confession to be under the judicial authority of God.   To be circumcised was ceremonially representative of gaining an entrance into that covenant community that had access in a specially revealed way to safe passage through the flaming swords of judgment into God's blessed presence.  \par }\pard \qj \fi360\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1530\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1530\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Genesis 9:11\par }\pard \qj \li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 In Genesis 9:11 the Genesis flood is referred to as a "cutting off of the flesh" curse of the covenant.  This is the same word "berith" used to depict God's covenant as signified in the OT by the cutting ceremony of circumcision.  Clearly, the water is here being related to circumcision as described in  Genesis 15, 17 and 22 where the  practice of circumcision is intended to}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  signify }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 the judicial authority of God's sword.  \par \par }\pard \qj \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Isaiah  43:1--4}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 This passage speaks of god's redemption in terms of passing through waters with God into salvation.  It prepares for the New Covenant use of water in baptism.\par }\pard \qj \li1440\ri720\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin720\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par 2 Peter 3:5-7 and 1 Peter 3:18-22\par }\pard \qj \li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Both relate the idea of judgment by water as observed in Genesis flood to the day of judgment.  But in 1 Peter 3:21, Peter states that "this water (referring to the flood) symbolizes }{\f25\fs20\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 baptism}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  that now saves you ...by the resurrection of Jesus Christ."  \par }\pard \qj \li2520\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1530\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1530\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1 Cor 10:1-2\par }\pard \qj \li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 In a similar fashion, the exodus through the Red Sea is spoken of by Paul in 1 Cor. 10:1-2 as a }{\f25\fs20\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 baptism}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  in water.  Paul writes,  "our fathers...all passed through the sea, and ... were baptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea." \par }\pard \qj \li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \fi360\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Colossians 2:11-12}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ,  New Testament Verification of dual OT sign: }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx3140\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The New Testament evidence for relating baptism to circumcision is supported by Colossians 2:11,12 where circumcision is used as an analogy for baptism.  In general, Paul is asserting that circumcision in its day signified the same realities which baptism signifies in the present day.  In essence, the "water" of baptism signifies the same reality as the "knife" in circumcision.  \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Our point of course is to notice that circumcision in its covenant context signified the same realities as baptism in our covenant context.  What about its function?  That Circumcision was BOTH a sign and a seal in the Old Covenant is clear if but by the explicit language of Paul to this point.  \par \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rom. 4:11}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 He received the }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 sign}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  of circumcision as a }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 seal}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  of the righteousness that he had by faith while he was still uncircumcised. The purpose was to make him the ancestor of all who believe without being circumcised and who thus have righteousness reckoned to them,  }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 12}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  and likewise the ancestor of the circumcised who are not only circumcised but who also follow the example of the faith that our ancestor Abraham had before he was circumcised.\par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par As a "seal" we see that circumcision transacted the covenant while also signifying the covenant.  Yet this didn't violate the Abrahamic principle of justification by faith then-- so why should it now?    (And of course, nor did it stop Abraham from giving it to infants on the eighth day after their birth.)  For if someone wanted to distinguish baptism from circumcision along the lines that baptism is more related to the faith of a believer in this sense-- clearly then they would need to be consistent and say this would hold true for circumcision if we read what Paul had to say about the matter. \par \par Here again, we discover continuity with circumcision.  We see  that circumcision, like baptism, is an initiatory rite or "entrance }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 sacrament}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ."  And so as expected, it is applied in a way that initiates, less renews/confirms, the covenant.  And this happens not so as to diminish justification by faith, but rather to initiate it as by the presence of God in His covenant community whereby he is actively saving the elect by his grace.   This is again all the more clear given the fact that baptism is clearly associated with circumcision by Paul. \par \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Col. 2:11}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par In him also you were circumcised with a spiritual circumcision, by putting off the body of the flesh in the circumcision of Christ;  }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 12}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  when you were buried with him in baptism, you were also raised with him through faith in the power of God, who raised him from the dead. \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par And again, we see the sacramental aspect of baptism in plain view as that which }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 like circumcision}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  not only represents salvation, but also functions in some sense to initiate/effect salvation.  We are said to be both buried and raised with him in baptism through faith in the power of God.   As noted earlier, here we have a case that if read temporally would place baptism as preceding faith.  My point is that the "temporal" reading is wrong in any case if in relation to faith necessarily.  Rather the point is that Baptism is related to effectual calling whereby a person is enabled to embrace Christ so as to be vicariously buried and raised with Christ before God.  Paul's point in Rom. 6 will then be that baptism as "effecting" our vicarious status with God will also  effect our manner of living before God.  Unfortunately, some have totally missed this point in trying to force Rom. 6 into teaching a profession of faith kind of precondition to the administration of baptism.  Rather we could just as well take this passage and exhort our children (as Paul is exhorting the church at large) to walk in newness of life as this includes a  credible profession of faith (what we will call a confirmed faith) in Christ.  This would be in perfect harmony with Paul's logic, as derived from the "seal" of baptism that effects salvation.   (AS any good preacher will do, Paul exhorted his readers to do that which he knew would happen only if God makes it happen by effectual calling.  And of course only God knows who are the elect such that the exhortation would be reciprocated with confirmed faith.)   See then how baptism is shown to "effect" our relation to Christ in his death and resurrection such that we are exhorted to live out this effect in newness of life. \par \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rom. 6:3}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Do you not know that all of us who have been baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into his death?  }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 4}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Therefore we have been buried with him by baptism into death, so that, just as Christ was raised from the dead by the glory of the Father, so we too might walk in newness of life. \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Summary: Whereas baptism is not the agent of salvation- this being Christ by the Holy Spirit in Effectual  Calling \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1Cor. 6:11}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  And this is what some of you used to be. But you were}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  washed}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 , you were sanctified, you were justified in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ and in the Spirit of our God. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Heb. 10:22}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  let us approach with a true heart in full assurance of faith, with our hearts sprinkled clean from an evil conscience and our bodies}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  washed}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  with pure water.\par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Titus 3:5}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par he saved us, not because of any works of righteousness that we had done, but according to his mercy, through the water of rebirth and renewal by the Holy Spirit. \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 New Testament baptism is the New Covenant entrance sacrament into the New Covenant Israel of God.   It, like the Lord's Supper, is a New covenant rite that both directs us to Christ and is used by the Holy Spirit as an instrument in salvation. \par }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls38\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Renewal Rite: (James Torrance, Worship, Community and The Triume God, exp chapter 1-3) \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1440\faauto\ls38\ilvl1\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 OT: Temple Sacrifice\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}NT: Lord\rquote s Supper\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Note Trajectory: \par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 a. Sacrifice in the Garden After the Fall Whereby The Elect are "Clothed" In Righteousness \par }\pard \qj \li1980\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1980\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Failed Human Attempt at "clothing"/Restoration--\par }\pard \ql \li2430\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2430\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 3:7 }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Then the eyes of both were opened, and they knew that they were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together and made loincloths for themselves.\par }\pard \ql \li1980\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1980\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 A Cover Up}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 -- }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 "Fig leaves... biggest leaves available in Canaan-- yet with heavy indentations, rough, brittle and still skimpy...  }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Images of inadequacy! \par }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Evidence of Failed Results: Still hiding from Creator, in whose presence they were created to live.\par }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 " and the man and his wife hid themselves from the presence of Yahweh God among the trees of the garden. }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  v. 10, "}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 I heard the sound of thee in the garden, and I was afraid, because I was naked; and I hid myself.".}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1980\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1980\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li2340\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx2340{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls5\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls5\adjustright\rin0\lin2340\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Divine "Clothing/Restoration Accomplished as through Judgment}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Next scene-- 8) }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 And they heard the voice of Yahweh God  walking in the garden  in regard to the spirit  (breeze) of the  day.\par }\pard \qj \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li2420\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx2420{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls6\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls6\adjustright\rin0\lin2420\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Divine Clothing/Restoration}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 And so notice the end, that whatever selse happens here, it will result in new clothing, even as this will be accomplished as through judgment! \par }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 (vs. 21) And the Yahweh God made garments (tunics)  of skins for the man and for his wife, and clothed them\par }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 They are clothed not with plants (and they sewed fig leaves together and made themselves aprons, v.7) but with animal skins, fore-shadowing the shedding of blood, the taking of life necessary to save Eve and Adam.\par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Covering through death of sacrificial animal. \par }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Evidently, God does not think much of the fig leaves; they don't adequately cover the shameful nakedness. Thus God in his grace takes matters into his own hand to provide a covering. \par \par Result: \par A re-establishment of covenant relationship, both between the man and his wife and between them and God.\par }\pard \qj \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj \fi-360\li2340\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx2340{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls7\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls7\adjustright\rin0\lin2340\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Provisional Expulsion -- vs. 23-24\par }\pard \qj \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 23 therefore the LORD God sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from which he was taken.  24 He drove out the man; and at the east of the garden of Eden he stationed the cherubim, and a sword flaming and turning to guard the way to the tree of life. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 like one of us... live forever...}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  \par --  through the probation-temptation, man had come to experience the full dimension of the conflict of good and evil, as celestial creature had previously known it... \par --punishment for such unworthy grasping of the sacramental tree of life would be to grant the covenanted exclusion from physical death and this would paradoxically, make men's state of death and alienation permanent, since reconciliation could come only by a sacrificial dying... \par --although man's expulsion from the garden mercifully forestalled that possibility the exile judgment was of course a manifestation of God's displeasure with fallen man... protection of the sanctuary was now assigned to being who elsewhere too are found as guardian s of God's throne (Ex. 25:18ff, 1 Ki.6:23) ... }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \qj \fi-360\li2340\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx2340{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls8\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls8\adjustright\rin0\lin2340\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Being "clothed" in Redemptive History as anticipating the ultimate sacrifice\par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 As begun by this story and this  Biblical Imagery of Covering-- all of salvation history is noted by such pictures of clothing, pictures whereby in human shame, God is the provider of covering... \par }\pard \ql \li2880\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 9:23 (Noah's nakedness covered)\par Is. 61:10 (garments of salvation, a robe of righteousness)\par Ezek. 16 (elaborate imagery of God's clothing naked Israel Zech. 3:1-5\par Mt. 22:11 (man without a wedding garment)\par Lk. 15:22 (robe place upon the prodigal son)\par Gal. 3:27 (we have "put on" Christ)\par }\pard \ql \li1980\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1980\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rev. 7:9}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525    After this I looked, and behold, a great multitude which no man could number, standing before the throne and before the Lamb, clothed in white robes, with palm branches in their hands, 7:13   Then one of the elders addressed me, saying, }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 "Who are these, clothed in white robes, and whence have they come?"  }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  14 I said to him, "Sir, you know." And he said to me, "These are they who have come out of the great tribulation; they have washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.\par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rev. 19:8}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  (fine linen=righteous deeds of saints)\par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rev. 22:14}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525    Blessed are those who wash their robes, that they may have the right to the tree of life and that they may enter the city by the gates.Application1. Living in a cursed world-Expectations must be realistic-We hide from God2. Living in hope of salvation.\par }\pard \ql \li1980\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1980\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Note also the following "clothing" language preceding the New Covenant: \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1Chr. 15:27 David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, as also were all the Levites who were carrying the ark, and the singers, and Chenaniah the leader of the music of the singers; and David wore a linen ephod. \par \par 2Chr. 6:41 \ldblquote Now rise up, O LORD God, and go to your resting place, you and the ark of your might. Let your priests, O LORD God, be clothed with salvation, and let your faithful rejoice in your goodness. \par \par }\pard \qj \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Pss. 132:13 \u182\'a6 For the LORD has chosen Zion; he has desired it for his habitation:  14 \ldblquote This is my resting place forever; here I will reside, for I have desired it.  ... 16 Its priests I will clothe with salvation, and its faithful will shout for joy.  17 There I will cause a horn to sprout up for David; I have prepared a lamp for my anointed one.  18 His enemies I will clothe with disgrace, but on him, his crown will gleam.\rdblquote \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 b. Sacrifice in the Patriarchial Period: \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx2250{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls9\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls9\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Cain & Abel-- \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 4:3}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par In the course of time Cain brought to the LORD an offering of the fruit of the ground,  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 4}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  and Abel for his part brought of the firstlings of his flock, their fat portions. And the LORD had regard for Abel and his offering,  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 5}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  but for Cain and his offering he had no regard. So Cain was very angry, and his countenance fell. \par \par }\pard \ql \li2880\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Evidently, there where already clear guidelines as to how God was to be worshipped, guidelines that required blood sacrifice as anticipating the Mosaic covenant...and ultimately Christ. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Note Hebrews 11:3,}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  "By faith Abel offered to God a more acceptable sacrifice than Cain" \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li2250\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx2250{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls10\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls10\adjustright\rin0\lin2250\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Noah\par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 8:20}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Then Noah built an}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  altar}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  to the LORD, and took of every clean animal and of every clean bird, and offered burnt offerings on the}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  altar}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 . \par \par }\pard \ql \li2880\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2880\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Sacrifice that satisfied God's anger... \par 1. burnt offering... pleasing smell -- indicating that God's anger was appeased by the substitutionary sacrifice.  In one sense we could say Noah's sacrifice pleased God so much as to cover a multitude of sins-- but of course ultimately this indicates God's grace in so far as he would appoint such a system... I.e. "ultimately, the acceptance of every sacrifice depends on God's  antecedent  gracious purpose, whereby he appointed  the sacrificial system as a means of atonement for reconciliation between God and man.  A fundamental principle of the Levitical law is "I have given the good for you upon the altar to make atonement for our souls. (Lev. 17:11) Clearly then Noah's sacrifice  is related to the special grace of God for a special covenant people-- as will be continue through Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, Moses, David, etc in the OC\par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \u-3913\'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx2160{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls11\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls11\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Abraham\par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 12:7}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Then the LORD appeared to Abram, and said, \ldblquote To your offspring I will give this land.\rdblquote  So he built there an}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  altar}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  to the LORD, who had appeared to him.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 8}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  From there he moved on to the hill country on the east of Bethel, and pitched his tent, with Bethel on the west and Ai on the east; and there he built an}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  altar}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  to the LORD and invoked the name of the LORD. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 13:4}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par to the place where he had made an}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  altar}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  at the first; and there Abram called on the name of the LORD. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 13:18}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par So Abram moved his tent, and came and settled by the oaks of Mamre, which are at Hebron; and there he built an}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  altar}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  to the LORD.\par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 22:2}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par He said, \ldblquote Take your son, your only son Isaac, whom you love, and go to the land of Moriah, and offer him there as a burnt offering on one of the mountains that I shall show you.\rdblquote   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 3}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  So Abraham rose early in the morning, saddled his donkey, and took two of his young men with him, and his son Isaac; he cut the wood for the burnt offering, and set out and went to the place in the distance that God had shown him. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 22:6}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Abraham took the wood of the burnt offering and laid it on his son Isaac, and he himself carried the fire and the knife. So the two of them walked on together.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 7}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Isaac said to his father Abraham, \ldblquote Father!\rdblquote  And he said, \ldblquote Here I am, my son.\rdblquote  He said, \ldblquote The fire and the wood are here, but where is the lamb for a burnt offering?\rdblquote   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 8}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Abraham said, \ldblquote God himself will provide the lamb for a burnt offering, my son.\rdblquote  So the two of them walked on together. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gen. 22:13}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par And Abraham looked up and saw a ram, caught in a thicket by its horns. Abraham went and took the ram and offered it up as a burnt offering instead of his son. \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af3\dbch\