 \ldblquote This is my body, which is given for you. Do this in remembrance of me.\rdblquote   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 20}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  And he did the same with the cup after supper, saying, \ldblquote This cup that is poured out for you is the new covenant in my blood.\par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Acts 2:42}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  They devoted themselves to the apostles' teaching and fellowship, to the breaking of bread and the prayers.}{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Acts 20:7}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  On the first day of the week, when we met to break bread, Paul was holding a discussion with them; since he intended to leave the next day, he continued speaking until midnight.\par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1Cor. 10:16}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  The cup of blessing that we bless, is it not a sharing in the blood of Christ? The bread that we break, is it not a sharing in the body of Christ? \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1Cor. 11:25}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  In the same way he took the cup also, after supper, saying, \ldblquote This cup is the new covenant in my blood. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.\rdblquote  \par }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1Cor. 11:27}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Whoever, therefore, eats the bread or drinks the cup of the Lord in an unworthy manner will be answerable for the body and blood of the Lord.\par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 God IS present in transacting and effecting His saving grace to us-- thus Christ's very real, albeit spiritual presence as mediated through a very real "means" or instrument as regulated by God rather than men.  This language includes "koinonia" (1 Cor. 10:16-17) as applied to the Lord's supper such that to eat the bread is to in some sense" participate" with Christ and be nourished/renewed by Him.   This surely makes more sense of Christ command to eat the bread and drink the wine and then to say "this IS my body\u8230\'c9 this IS my blood." (John  )   It would be a stretch it seems to see in this language merely the idea of  "represent or signify" regarding our fellowship with Christ without actually effecting our fellowship with Christ.   \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls38\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Sabbath: (c.f. Lee Iron\rquote s \ldblquote The Eschatological Sabbath\rdblquote  in recommended readings) \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1440\faauto\ls38\ilvl1\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 OT: Day 7 (First Creation \ldblquote rest\rdblquote )- temporally executed\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}NT: Day 1 (Second Creation \ldblquote rest)\emdash spiritually executed\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }{\b\f25\fs22\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Two Often Misunderstood Categories Illustrated:  \par }{\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742