rsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Patriarchal Era:}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Both }{\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Pre-Typological and Spiritual Aspects\par }\pard \ql \li1620\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1620\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Law: Gen.17:1, 9\par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Evidently, there is one level of fulfillment that is relative to human obedience and another level that is not.  Paul's point is that the Mosaic covenant did not annul that aspect revealed to Abraham after the principle of God's sovereign grace.  Here again, the context is important, for while "human obligation" is required in any covenant by the definition of a covenant itself, God has taken upon himself to secure those human obligations so that those chosen of God might then have access to the covenant promises.  This was the point earlier in Genesis 15.\par }\pard \ql \li1620\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1620\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gospel: 15:7ff \par }\pard\plain \s20\ql \li2520\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 \f2\fs20\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The smoking firepot and blazing torch are symbols of God, even as he appeared later as a pillar of cloud and a pillar of fire, even as his presence on Mt. Sinai was accompanied by smoke and fire.  So here God himself, after making his promise to Abram, cuts a covenant by walking through the carcasses. And as God walks through the dead animals, it is God who will guarantee the covenant-- it is God who will make the payments, and who then here takes the oath such as to invoke curse upon himself if payments are not made in full-- it is God who will suffer our part-- and it is God who is the sole guarantor of this covenant-- a covenant as initiated to Adam and his descendents through Seth, ratified to Noah and his descendants through Shem, her ratified to Abram as through his descendents, even one born as from his own body!  So what exactly was God guaranteeing?  IF viewed from the lens of the New Covenant, we see that the "land" is symbolic of "heaven." (Heb. 11:8)\par \par }{\b\f25\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard\plain \ql \li1080\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 \f5\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\f25\fs20\ul\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Mosaic Covenant\par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Law: (as applied Typologically to temporal blessings) \par }\pard \ql \li3240\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin3240\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  \par }\pard \ql \li2520\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 4)   }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Sanctions }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 (contractual consequences)}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li3240\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin3240\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\ul\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Blessings}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 : Gen. 2:17b implied with Gen.3:5, vs.22 especially, Exod. 20:6, 12; Deut. 28:1-14\par }\pard \ql \fi720\li2520\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin2520\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Curses: Gen. 2:17b, 3:5, Exod. 20:5; Deut. 28:15-68\par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\