ny brethren. \par 1Cor. 11:1   Be imitators of me, as I am of Christ.  \par Eph. 5:1   Therefore be imitators of God, as beloved children, \par Mt. 5:44   But I say to you, Love your enemies and pray for those who persecute you,   45 so that you may be children of your Father in heaven; for he makes his sun rise on the evil and on the good, and sends rain on the righteous and on the unrighteous.  \par Matt. 5:48  Therefore you are to be perfect, as your heavenly Father is perfect.\par Jn. 13:34   I give you a new commandment, that you love one another. Just as I have loved you, you also should love one another}{\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \u-3844\'fc\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1800\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1800\faauto\ls31\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Sermon on the Mount: (Mt. 5ff )\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \u-3844\'fc\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li2160\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx2160\faauto\ls30\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Apostolic Commandments (Rom.12ff, Eph. 4-6, etc)}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\i\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gospel: \par {\listtext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \u-3880\'d8\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1080\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080\faauto\ls27\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Grace Promise: \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\tx1080\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 By Christ Concerning HImself: \par }{\b\f25\fs20\ul\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Matt. 5:17}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par \ldblquote Do not think that I have come to abolish the law or the prophets; I have come not to abolish but to fulfill.  }{\b\f25\fs20\ul\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 18}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  For truly I tell you, until heaven and earth pass away, not one letter, not one stroke of a letter, will pass from the law until all is accomplished}{\f25\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 . \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 By the Apostles concerning Christ: \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Gal. 3:15-17}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Brothers and sisters, I give an example from daily life: once a person's will has been ratified, no one adds to it or annuls it.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 16}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Now the promises were made to Abraham and to his offspring; it does not say, \ldblquote And to offsprings,\rdblquote  as of many; but it says, \ldblquote And to your }{\f25\fs20\ul\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 offspring}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ,\rdblquote  that is, to }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 one person, who is Christ.}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 17}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  My point is this: the law, which came four hundred thirty years later, does not annul a covenant previously ratified by God, so as to nullify the promise.  }{\b\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 18}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  For if the inheritance comes from the law, it no longer comes from the promise; but God granted it to Abraham through the promise. \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\ul\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Eph. 3:6}{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par that is, the Gentiles have become fellow heirs, members of the same body, and sharers in the }{\f25\fs20\cf17\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 promise }{\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 in Christ Jesus through the gospel.\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 .\par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Summary:  The grace promise (As Paul refers to it as "promise" not "covenant") is added to the "works covenant" so as to satisfy God's covenant/legal requirements in order to receive the covenant blessings, this as accomplished by Christ.   There is in short a temporal aspect to the Mosaic covenant that has ceased, even as there is an eternal aspect of the Mosaic covenant in continuity with the promise made to Abraham and even Adam before him that remains as fulfilled by Christ.  For when God promised a "seed" who would guarantee the creation covenant stipulation on behalf of the elect, this was again ratified to Abraham in the covenant rite of the slain animals.  This promise did not annul the creation covenant based upon works, it merely added to this creation covenant the promise of substitution whereby God's grace would be revealed so as to be in harmony with his justice.  We should not then think in terms of "covenant of grace" vs. "covenant of works"-- rather we should think in terms of a COVENANT between God and humanity, a covenant that we have broken by our willful disobedience such as to deserve the curse of the covenant.  This covenant was never annulled.  Rather God added to the covenant a promise to meet its demands on behalf of those chose by his sovereign grace}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par {\listtext\pard\plain\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \hich\af25\dbch\af0\loch\f25 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls41\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Temple\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs22\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 NOT: Visible Temple vs. No Visible Temple (Old vs. New) \par RATHER: Bethel to Tabernacle to Jerusalem (Geographical/Civil/Mosaic)  Temple vs. Apostolic/Ecclesial/Non-Geo/poltical temple.  \par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The trajectory of a }{\b\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Mediated}{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  presence of God unto Salvation-- The Succession of "Tabernacle"  \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 In redemptive-history, ever since Adam and his posterity were excommunicated from "before the face of God" (Gen.3:8) until the elect are reunited back into God's immediate presence (as told in Revelations 21:3-4 using language derived from Leviticus 26:9ff), God has in a provisional way }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 mediated}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  his saving presence as through divinely appointed sacramental rituals, governments and confessions in every redemptive era.   \line \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\i\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Rev. 21:1-4}{\i\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  Now I saw a new heaven and a new earth, for the first heaven and the first earth had passed away. Also there was no more sea.  Then I, John, saw the holy city, New Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband. And I heard a loud voice from heaven saying,  "Behold, the }{\i\f25\fs20\ul\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 tabernacle}{\i\f25\fs20\cf1\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  of God is with men, and He will dwell with them, and they shall be His people. God Himself will be with them and be their God. "And God will wipe away every tear from their eyes; there shall be no more death, nor sorrow, nor crying. There shall be no more pain, for the former things have passed away.''}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par King David certainly understood the omnipresence of God in the world, yet he still longed for that }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 saving}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  presence that was mediated through the ordinances and worship of the old covenant.}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 (Pss. 84:2)  Orthodoxy in the Old Testament era was described in terms like "dwelling place", "living God", "tabernacle" even as covenants where initiated and sealed through rites whereby God manifested his presence to his people..}{\cs17\f25\fs20\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \s18\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f5\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs17\fs18\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   See for example Gen.15, 26:24, Exodus 29:42 where the tabernacle is also described as the "dwelling place" of God in Deuteronomy 12:5. See also Ex. 29:42, 40:34, Lev. 22:3, Ps.76.2, Pss 76:2, Num.35:34}}}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  The New Covenant, although under new apostolic forms, proves no exception as promised by Christ in Matthew 28:18-20, " I am with you until the end of the age." For in the words of Calvin about the Lord's table in the context of authorized confessions and government, "his word cannot lie or deceive us: Take, eat, drink: this is my body which is given for you; this is my blood which is shed for forgiveness of sins..."}{\cs17\f25\fs20\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn {\footnote \pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f5\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs17\fs18\up6\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \chftn }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  See John Calvin, }{\i\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Institutes, }{\f25\fs18\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Book.IV. Chapter.7.1,3,5) }}}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   I am tempted at this point to reclaim the clich\u233\'8e "full gospel"-- as developed in Ephesians where "Christ fills all in all."  And clearly what is }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 not}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  meant}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 here is the filling by an individualized Holy Spirit, but rather that kind of filling that is explicitly stated in the passage, "for the church which is his body\u8230\'c9" (Eph.1:22, see also Eph.2:19-22 and then Eph.4:10ff)  This church made visible in its sacramental worship, confession and pastoral oversight. (see 1 Tim.1-3)\par \par This trajectory of "presence" theology is manifest along several trajectories-- note especially  the sacramental rites as noted below. For now, see how this can be traced as through the concept of "place" as in every redemptive epoch is central to the gospel. \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 3.   The trajectory of a Tabernacle Beginning with Creation's "Garden": \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 a. The Garden: \par }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Beginning from the creation account itself, to the ark under the Noahic context, to Bethel under the Patriarchial context, to the tabernacle under the Mosaic context and finally to the church itself under the new covenant context-- there has been a "place" whereby God in a special way makes himself present for the sake of transacting the covenant.  \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The description of Creation Establishes the garden itself as God's habitat-- God the  Ruler of all things.  Creates a royal dwelling where He may  govern:\par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Presence theology-- the cosmic structure was built as a habitation for the Creator himself.  Heaven and earth were erected as a house of God, a palace of the Great King, the seat of sovereignty of the Lord of the covenant.   \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Is. 37:16  "O Lord of hosts, God of Israel, the One who dwells between the cherubim, You are God, You alone, of all the }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 kingdoms}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525  of the earth. You have made }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 heaven and earth}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 . \par }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Isa. 66:1 }{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Thus says the LORD: "Heaven is my throne  and the earth is my footstool; what is the house which you  would build for me, and what is the place of my rest?\par Heb.  4:13, And before him no creature is hidden, but all are open  and laid bare to the eyes of him with whom we have to do.\par \par }\pard \qj \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Therefore, creation was  a royal construction of a place for God-- the center of a Kingdom!}{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \qj \li1170\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1170\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Notice also the Clear references to tabernacle when Adam And Eve are expulsed: \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 1."expulsion" -- languaged used for "excommunication"  under old covenant system\par }\pard \qj \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 2. flaming swords and cherubim-- guarded the inner sanctuary of the tabernacls (curtain) and placed over the ark of cov.\par 3. to the east of the garden-- this was the direction facing the entrance to the temple... }{\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\b\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 b. The Noahic "Tabernacle" -- The Ark of Salvation \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Amazing attention and detail is given to the construction and inhabitants of an ark-- somehow, whatever this episode of redemptive history is about-- it is focused on an ark! \par This Heb. word for "ark" occurs only one other time in the OT-- would you want to guess there that is?  \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Exodus 2:3, 5-- the basket in which baby Moses was hidden\par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 What did that basket represent then but God's divine intervention for safe passage into the salvation planned for Isreal.  \par \par This ark-- whereas it is not responsible for saving Noah and Moses, was the means of grace given by God in order to affect his decree to save his special elect people from destruction.  \par This ark for Moses later-- was safe passage as against the political and military might of Eqypt against Israel-- it was safe passage as against Pharoh's decree that all first born should be destroyed-- it was the "safe-house" that protected nothing less than God's representative who would deliver his people from destruction into a promised land! \par \par Here-- it is the safe-house for Noah and those under his jurisdiction... -- it was safe passage as through the judgment waters  of God's wrath-- having the dual effect of both destruction and salvation-- destroying those who  after the line of Cain would bring destruction upon the line of Seth-- saving the elect from extinction at the hands of the  "giants"-- those who through political might would bring destruction to the line of Seth-- who after the line of Cain were apostate and antagonistic to the religion of Yahweh!  \par \par What are we to think of this ark if according to the author's intention?\par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 A.  House of god-- building a house (14-16)\par All the features mentioned in the description of the ark belong to the architecture of a house-- Rooms, a door, three stories, roof/window. More like a house than a boat.  To be out of this house is to be under God's judgment. To be in this house is to have found a save haven, a place of refuge.  Such as to be in the ark is to be members of a household! \par }\pard \ql \li1160\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 A safe-house-- \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 In Gen.7:16-- "Yahweh shut him in"-- an act of unequal protection on the part of God.. this being eluded to by Isaiah in 26:20-- BOTH TURN OUT TO be dealing with the enclosure of God's people in a passage through death that proves to be a refuge from God's wrath... \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Of what does this "house" correspond to in scripture... was the author saying anything theological by the description itself... as it turns out-- very clearly so...\par \par b. Second Cosmic House:  \par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 You will remember that creation itself was described as a kind of "house of God" whereby God was its chief inhabitant and grand architect...\par }\pard \ql \fi360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Heb. 11:10 refers to heaven as the city whose architect and builder is God.\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par Here, the story is clearly wanting to describe A }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 New}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525   Creation as the "new house of God" -- (through first the destruction of an old creation) \par }\pard \ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \par }\pard \ql \li1080\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 Therefore, as we will see, the Ark-- represented  the new kingdom of God-- a symbol of the creations cosmic house, the church and then heaven.. \par Quick review of the Textual evidence: \par }\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \bullet \tab apart from Creation, the flood is the only event in the primeval history to be dated\par \bullet \tab the account of the flood is given very carefully in sevens... \par }\pard \ql \li1800\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 7 days of waiting for the flood (7:4)\par 7 days of wating for  the flood (7:10)\par 7 days wait after the flood (8:10) \par 7 days wait after the flood (8:12) \par }\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \bullet \tab the "earth" is mentioned six times vs. 6:11-13 and the verb "to ruin" (spoil or destroy) is applied 5 times... i.e. the destruction of the old creatoin... \par \bullet \tab }{\i\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 And God saw}{\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 ... (vs.12)the last time these exact words are used was in Gen. 1:31-- whre God "saw that all was very good" in contrast to \par \bullet \tab the description of animals in entering the ark in 14-16 echoes of the creation account (male and female 1:27, "according to their types (1:11, 12, 21, 24, 25).\par \bullet \tab So too, the description of destruction of all living things in 7:19-25--at first very general is gradually made more specific--The sequence of "birds, land animals, creeping things" in harmony with 1:20-24) and with the almost the same exact language...  \par \bullet \tab Notice too the "ruach" (Spirit) of God in Gen. 1:2 and this same ruach passing over the waters at the critical junction described in Gen. 8:1.. as with the formation of the new creation. \par \bullet \tab the command given to Noah realitive to eating 6:21-22 exchoes the creation commands about eating-- "you and they will have it to eat" (1:29-30) \par \bullet \tab the architectural features of the ark-house match up with the features in creations cosmic house as that is figuratively envisaged in various biblical passages... \par }\pard \ql \li1880\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1880\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 -- 3 stories of th ark correspond to the three stories of th world conceptualized as divided into the heaven above, the earth beneath and the sphere under the earth associated especially with waters-- this as corresponding to the three categories of creatures noted above who where the 3 spheres "governors" \par -- clearly, the "window" of the ark as located along the top of the arkis the counterpart to the "window of heaven" refereed to in this very narrative in 7:11, 8:2.  \par }\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \bullet \tab And like creation itself-- it is God who reveals the design of the house\par \bullet \tab a literary parellelism that is patterned after the literary parrelelism of creation... (see Kline p.154) \par }\pard \ql \li1980\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1980\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 The 6  "days"\par a. Light/darkness--removing canopy, 8.13\par b.  Waters  above/below--restraining of waters, 8.2\par c. Dryland emerges-- dryland emerges, 8.3-6, 6-11\par d. Luminaries--(possibly) 8.13,  removing canopy\par e. Living creatures--living creatures,  finally Noah\par f. same on sixth day as on fifth\par }\pard \ql \li2160\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2160\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 -- what is depicted in days five and six of the creation narrative (1:24-31) corresponds to the emergence from the ark onto the dry land of the living creatures in language reminiscent of the creation story in 8:15-19) \par }\pard \ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid742525 {\f25\fs20\insrsid742525\charrsid742525 \bullet \tab This then leading to the "Sabbath" rest of day seven as corresponding to the closing scene in 8:20 ff by Noah's priestly role taking pleasure and consecrating to God all of what now is the new creation... \par \bullet